{
  "title": "CoreDataStack logs errors with print() instead of DebugLogger",
  "description": "`Ramekin/CoreDataStack.swift` uses `print(...)` for Core \
Data load / save failures. Everything else in the app routes through \
`DebugLogger.shared` and surfaces in the in-app debug viewer. Swap to \
`DebugLogger.shared.log` so a user reporting sync issues can actually hand us \
the Core Data error in the log dump.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
